# Month end — signed up to auxiliary pioneer, missed the hours. Brother
# Phillips' "encouragement" (dialogue-context.md § 10: the verb for what is
# functionally a reprimand). Kind, and corrective.
# TODO: authenticity check — month-end draft.

join elder_coordinator (neutral) at center
You hand your report slip across the literature counter. Brother Phillips reads it, and then reads it again.
elder_coordinator (neutral): {GameState.player_title} {GameState.player_name}. Could I borrow you for a minute?
He walks you back to the library room and leaves the door open a hand's width.
elder_coordinator (neutral): Nobody's upset. I want you to hear that first.
elder_coordinator (neutral): But you put your name to thirty hours. When we make a promise to Jehovah, we want to keep it. You understand.
elder_coordinator (neutral): Next month, you might consider sitting down with your calendar on the first Sunday. Write the hours in before the month fills up.
- "I'll do better next month."
	[signal arg="STANDING:elders:1"]
	elder_coordinator (neutral): I know you will.
- "I don't know if I can do thirty."
	[signal arg="EXPOSE:1"]
	elder_coordinator (neutral): Then pray about what you can do. Jehovah doesn't ask more of us than we have.
	He smiles, and pats the doorframe on his way out, as if the room had done something right.
leave elder_coordinator
